{
    "@visokiotype": "CustomBlockSchema.CustomBlockManifest",
    "name": "Google BigQuery Import Table",
    "scriptFilename": "script.py",
    "language": "PYTHON",
    "executableVersion": null,
    "minVersions": [
        null
    ],
    "optionsVersion": 1,
    "apiVersion": "VERSION_0",
    "isResourceIntensiveScript": false,
    "showPartitioning": false,
    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Reads a whole Google BigQuery table or view, page by page, with BigQuery's types mapped to Omniscope field types.",
    "category": "Connectors",
    "subcategory": "BigQuery",
    "tags": [
        "google",
        "bigquery",
        "import",
        "table",
        "google cloud",
        "connector"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Reads every record of a Google BigQuery table (or view) into the workflow.\n\n**How to set it up**\n\n1. Create a service account in Google Cloud with the roles it needs (BigQuery Data Viewer on the table; for a view, also BigQuery Job User on the project), and download a JSON key for it. Save the key file on the Omniscope server, outside any shared folder.\n2. Choose the key file in **JSON key file**, or leave it empty if the server already has Google credentials (the `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` environment variable, or the service account of a Google Cloud machine).\n3. Enter the **Table ID**: `project.dataset.table`.\n\nTables are read directly, page by page, which BigQuery does not bill as a query. Views, materialised views and external tables are read with `SELECT *`, which is billed as a query. NUMERIC values arrive as decimals, DATE as dates, TIME as text, arrays, STRUCT and JSON values as JSON text.",
    "dependencies": "google-cloud-bigquery\npyarrow\ndb-dtypes",
    "options": [
        {
            "name": "ApplicationCredentials",
            "title": "JSON key file",
            "description": "Optional. The path, on the Omniscope server, of a service account's JSON key file. Leave empty to use the server's own Google credentials (the GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS environment variable, or the service account of the machine it runs on).",
            "groupTitle": "Connection",
            "width": "ONE",
            "@visokiotype": "CustomBlockSchema.FileCustomBlockPublicOption",
            "mandatory": false,
            "defaultValue": null,
            "readOnly": true
        },
        {
            "name": "TableId",
            "title": "Table ID",
            "description": "The table's ID: project.dataset.table, for example my-project.sales.orders. A view works too.",
            "groupTitle": "Table",
            "width": "ONE",
            "@visokiotype": "CustomBlockSchema.TextCustomBlockPublicOption",
            "mandatory": true,
            "defaultValue": null
        },
        {
            "name": "PageSize",
            "title": "Page size",
            "description": "Records per request (default 10,000). Larger pages mean fewer requests and more memory per page. All pages are read whatever the size.",
            "groupTitle": "Advanced",
            "width": "HALF",
            "@visokiotype": "CustomBlockSchema.IntegerCustomBlockPublicOption",
            "numMin": 1,
            "numMax": null,
            "mandatory": false,
            "defaultValue": null,
            "showAsSlider": false
        },
        {
            "name": "MaxRows",
            "title": "Maximum records",
            "description": "Optional. Read only the first this many records, for example to try out a large table. Empty or 0 reads them all.",
            "groupTitle": "Advanced",
            "width": "HALF",
            "@visokiotype": "CustomBlockSchema.IntegerCustomBlockPublicOption",
            "numMin": 0,
            "numMax": null,
            "mandatory": false,
            "defaultValue": null,
            "showAsSlider": false
        }
    ],
    "blockOutputs": [
